    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p>An insulating glove with an embedded <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Energy_Cell\" title=\"Energy Cell\">Energy Cell</a>, the Stunning Gauntlet produces an electrifying charge when it strikes a target. A Stunning Gauntlet changes the wearer's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Unarmed_Attacks\" title=\"Unarmed Attacks\">Unarmed Attacks</a> to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Stun\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Stun\">Stun</a> damage, and they provide a +1 bonus to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Stun\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Stun\">Stun</a> damage on a successful <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Unarmed_Attack\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Unarmed Attack\">Unarmed Attack</a>. </p><p>A Stunning Gauntlet is two sizes smaller than their wearer (for example, a Stunning Gauntlet designed for a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Human\" title=\"Human\">Human</a> are Tiny). Because of how they are worn, a Stunning Gauntlet can't be <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Disarmed\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Disarmed\">Disarmed</a> or dropped. </p><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Small_Stunning_Gauntlets\">Small Stunning Gauntlets</span></h3><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Medium_Stunning_Gauntlets\">Medium Stunning Gauntlets</span></h3>",
